WEBVTT

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:13.419
Our eyes on the ground where Port Targit is in smallville, sir.

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:17.100
Not schedule.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:01:07.900
So what are you in the mood for?

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:16.790
I'm in the mood. Just not for breakfast.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:25.730
Lois.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.299
The bedroom's upstairs.

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:31.299
Mm-hmm.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:33.299
But the port swing?

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:47.200
It's out there.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.200
Target is on the move.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.959
He sat in for the camp farm.

00:01:51.959 --> 00:02:01.189
Target closing in on farmhouse.

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:12.750
Daddy.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.750
General Lane.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:19.620
And Lucy.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.620
Happy Turkey Day, sis.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.620
Great.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.620
The whole Lane family's together for the holidays.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:03:28.939
Nervous, your dad just wants to spend time with you.

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:31.939
Oh, I think he's more interested in doing recon on the man dating his daughter,

00:03:31.939 --> 00:03:33.939
so hopefully someone's monogram jacket has vanished.

00:03:33.939 --> 00:03:34.939
I took care of it.

00:03:34.939 --> 00:03:35.939
Look, your dad's met me before.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:39.939
Before we were a couple, Clark, none of my other boyfriends have ever survived the general assault.

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:41.939
I'll be fine.

00:03:41.939 --> 00:03:45.939
Fine? Fine won't pass inspection. You have to be perfect.

00:03:45.939 --> 00:03:48.939
It is important to me that my dad likes you.

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:50.939
And it's important to me that you are happy.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:51.939
There's nothing to worry about.

00:03:51.939 --> 00:03:57.349
Except maybe if he finds out that you're a superhero.

00:03:57.349 --> 00:03:59.349
My dad hates superheroes.

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:07.620
Hey!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.300
Made yourself at home, Daddy.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.300
Your sister's still upstairs unpacking. She could be all day.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.300
It's good to see you, sir.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:27.810
So, nothing has changed around here.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.810
The mother still own the place.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.810
It is in her name, but I...

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.810
I see. You live in your mother's house,

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.810
and you work in a basement. Is that correct?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.810
Well, it is that correct?

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.810
the bullpen at the Daily Planet.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.620
I work side by side with Lois.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.620
She seems to write more articles than you.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.620
What exactly do you do with your time, Clark?

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.629
Hey, Daddy, Clark and I work together a lot.

00:04:54.629 --> 00:05:01.839
He just gives me the byline sometimes, and that's just how sweet he is.

00:05:01.839 --> 00:05:02.839
You look after each other.

00:05:02.839 --> 00:05:06.839
Good. Because if Lois is going to be spending any time around here.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:10.839
I've had a look around, and there's a few things that are going to have to be brought up the code.

00:05:10.839 --> 00:05:17.990
Scrubbing the bathroom tile with a toothbrush.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.990
That's number 17 on the list.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:27.629
Is you're not kidding?

00:05:27.629 --> 00:05:29.629
No, I never do.

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:32.629
Though I feel a little uncomfortable inspecting the enemy camp,

00:05:32.629 --> 00:05:37.629
your mother is my major opposition in the Senate.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:40.629
Does this mean you're finally running for office, Daddy?

00:05:40.629 --> 00:05:43.629
No, sweetheart. I'm the senior military advisor on a new bill,

00:05:43.629 --> 00:05:46.629
the Vigilante Registration Act.

00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:48.629
And by Vigilante, you mean...

00:05:48.629 --> 00:05:49.629
Vigilantes?

00:05:49.629 --> 00:05:53.629
Weekend warriors and masks. You run around inciting anarchy.

00:05:53.629 --> 00:05:54.629
Well, I don't think they incite anarchy.

00:05:54.629 --> 00:06:01.120
anarchy, they stop crime, protect people.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.120
And they commit acts of terrorism.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.120
Like the Ario Tower and Metropolis,

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.120
blown to kingdom come.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.120
No evidence of explosives.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.120
You want to know why?

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.120
Because one of them super freaks did it.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.120
You know what?

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.120
Hey, Daddy, since we're pretending it's a holiday,

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.120
what say we make it official,

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.120
and take a furlough from work?

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.120
Clark, do you know who the real heroes of the world are?

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.120
The men and women of our armed forces,

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.120
they have to enlist, go through background checks, training,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.120
training, through our rules, be held accountable for their actions.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.120
People start believing in these so-called superheroes.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.120
Pretty soon the superheroes start taking the law into their own hands.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.120
I will not let them compromise our national security.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:51.540
Phyllis, what do you think?

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.540
I think we need some veggies with our starches.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:59.670
baked or mashed.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.670
Whatever their general would like, of course.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:22.639
You know, when you need first aid, you expect it to be in the first place you look.

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:27.639
It's over here.

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:29.639
over here.

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:31.639
Look this, new chairs.

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:33.639
You had a whole new setup going on.

00:07:33.639 --> 00:07:34.639
You know, when I said you could move in,

00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:36.639
I didn't think you'd actually move in.

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:41.870
Take off your shirt.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.870
Like I haven't seen it all before.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:56.850
Looks like you had a rough night.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:57.850
Yeah.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.850
Somewhere between chasing the bad guy and dodging the press,

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:04.850
I ran into someone who literally had an axe to grind.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.850
That sounds like some serious overtime.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:10.850
But if I remember correctly, your cure-all was two raw eggs and a Belgian beer.

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.850
and beer, hmm?

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.850
Yeah, let me tell you something, Tess.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.850
I can do this whole nine to five thing with you, all right.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.850
But I draw the line at Happy Hour.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:28.300
How did you say you hurt yourself again?

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.300
It's just your typical hackswielding maniac.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.629
That's the surface.

00:08:35.629 --> 00:08:37.629
Something's happening beneath the surface.

00:08:37.629 --> 00:08:39.629
Your skin is reacting to the iodine.

00:08:39.629 --> 00:08:46.049
It's a sub-dermal tattoo.

00:08:46.049 --> 00:08:50.350
Oliver, I've seen this before.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.350
This is the signal for the suicide squad.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.350
Suicide squad, huh?

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.350
That's a hell of a name?

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.350
They're a hell of a team.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:58.350
When I was working for Amanda Waller,

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.350
at Checkmate, there were certain dirty jobs

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.350
that a government agent just couldn't do, not even us.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.350
And Waller would send in a squad.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.350
They were led by Rick Flagg.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.350
But they all died when Checkmate was attacked.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.350
Wait a second. Wait a second. I know this guy.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.350
This guy tied me to a cherry, beat me to a pulp,

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.350
and then he wanted to kiss and make up.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:23.389
I knew he got under my skin, but come on.

00:09:23.389 --> 00:09:25.389
Wait, Flag survived?

00:09:25.389 --> 00:09:27.389
He's recruiting a whole new squad.

00:09:27.389 --> 00:09:29.389
I politely declined.

00:09:29.389 --> 00:09:30.389
If he tagged you, he's tracking you.

00:09:30.389 --> 00:09:34.789
He's tracking you.

00:09:34.789 --> 00:09:45.909
Something tells me I'm not the only one.

00:09:45.909 --> 00:09:51.740
The fire has broken out at a refinery in Smallville.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.740
Clark should see this.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.740
Remind him what a real hero is.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.740
Hey, they were all the cranberries.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:05.240
This store must have had a fire sale, huh, Clark?

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:17.320
Where's Clark?

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.320
He went upstairs.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:24.100
Leave you holding the bags?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:36.220
What happened to be in a gentleman, hmm?

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.220
Leave it to the blur to turn a fire into a far

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:42.779
I found the cranberries in the truck.

00:10:42.779 --> 00:10:44.779
Where were they, honey?

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:45.779
Under the hood.

00:10:45.779 --> 00:10:59.929
I thought you said that Clark went upstairs.

00:10:59.929 --> 00:11:02.929
Yeah, he was upstairs.

00:11:02.929 --> 00:11:03.929
Outside.

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:05.929
Checking the chimney.

00:11:05.929 --> 00:11:06.929
Thanks.

00:11:06.929 --> 00:11:15.000
Excuse me.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:23.110
It's not a good time.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:25.110
You're where?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:29.700
I'll be right there.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:37.240
Lois, I need to go chop some wood.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.240
Give me a workup on Clark Kent.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.240
Kent, Kilawack, November, Tango.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.240
He's hiding something.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:12:05.610
That's exactly what I was afraid of.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:06.610
Fleg's tracking me, too.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.610
Which is a bit surprising, considering your impermeable skin.

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:11.610
You must have used blue kryptonite.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.610
Oliver, we have to figure out why he's tracking us.

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:17.610
Yeah, Tessa's working on that back at Watch Tower, which...

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.610
I appreciate the help.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.610
But she's run around there like she owns a building.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.610
If it wasn't for her, we wouldn't know about these tattoos.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.610
We wouldn't even be on Flag's trail.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:36.990
on Flag's trail. You gotta go.

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:40.620
What, the window? What are we 16?

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:48.960
No. Lucy? Lucy.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:52.779
Lucy.

00:12:52.779 --> 00:12:54.779
Did I hear you up here talking to someone, Clark?

00:12:54.779 --> 00:12:56.779
No. Just me.

00:12:56.779 --> 00:12:58.779
Good.

00:12:58.779 --> 00:13:00.779
Because I only brought one lemonade.

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:02.779
I thought you could use the refreshment.

00:13:02.779 --> 00:13:10.610
Thanks.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:17.149
The general give you a list.

00:13:17.149 --> 00:13:18.149
Yeah, I'm afraid so.

00:13:18.149 --> 00:13:21.620
He likes to test Lois' boyfriends.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.620
He's commenced they all have something to hide.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:34.110
So far, no one's passed.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.110
I'll be the first.

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:40.960
Well, if anyone can do it, I'm sure you can.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:48.509
You've grown into quite a man in the past six years, Clark.

00:13:48.509 --> 00:13:54.860
I'm sure Lois could use your help.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.860
I think I've earned a ten-minute break.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:58.860
Lucy?

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:02.240
Well, at least show me around the barn.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.240
It was really not much to see.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:09.269
Really?

00:14:09.269 --> 00:14:13.350
Lois, your sister just...

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.350
Ambushed you.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:19.759
Well, this has Lucy written all over it.

00:14:19.759 --> 00:14:22.759
In back-sabbing bitchberry lip gloss.

00:14:22.759 --> 00:14:23.759
You.

00:14:23.759 --> 00:14:24.759
Come with me.

00:14:24.759 --> 00:14:36.710
Lois, not so tight.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:37.710
So, so what?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.710
You thought I would catch you two tongue wrestling, and then what?

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.710
Have a big fight with Clark?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.710
Oh, is that? Just save it.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:48.710
Now, the only reason that I am keeping you around is for Dad.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:51.710
So go make yourself useful and get us some ice.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.710
There's ice in the freezer.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.710
Dad likes crushed.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:15:17.940
Chop and stack, one quarter wood.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:19.940
Sir, yes, sir.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.860
Careful Dad doesn't catch you making with the comments.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:28.590
You're catchy making with the Kung Fu there, Paul Bunyan.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:31.590
I'm sorry about what happened with Lucy.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:38.389
It wasn't your fault.

00:15:38.389 --> 00:15:44.090
Still, you can put out a burning building, but you can't contain her hot lips.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:52.740
She surprised me.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:57.889
You know what's a bigger surprise is that you couldn't stand up to your dad,

00:15:57.889 --> 00:15:59.889
unless you actually agree with this vigilante registration act.

00:15:59.889 --> 00:16:07.309
I am just trying to get through this holiday without a fight.

00:16:07.309 --> 00:16:10.309
Lois, you either agree with them or you don't.

00:16:10.309 --> 00:16:11.309
I don't.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:14.590
But this means something to the general, so please do not make me.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:16.590
Please do not make me choose sides.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.590
I thought you were somebody who stood up for what she believed in.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:22.590
And then when it comes to your father, you do the same thing that he does.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.590
You make your choices based on fear.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:25.590
Hey, just because you don't have a...

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.379
What, Lois?

00:16:28.379 --> 00:16:30.379
What you're going to say, father?

00:16:30.379 --> 00:16:40.950
What I am trying to say is that you haven't had to deal with a family for a really long time.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:43.950
All you have to answer to is yourself.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:48.950
Clark, if you want to be with me, you're going to have to deal with my family too.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.950
I hope you can respect that.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.950
You can respect that.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:17:12.359
I'm surprised the general's daughter would leave herself open to attack.

00:17:12.359 --> 00:17:17.529
Always watch your six, Miss Lane.

00:17:17.529 --> 00:17:20.829
Who are you?

00:17:20.829 --> 00:17:25.829
I'm sorry, I'm, uh, Colonel Richard Stafford.

00:17:25.829 --> 00:17:28.829
I'm sorry if I startled you.

00:17:28.829 --> 00:17:31.829
I'm posted nearby at Fort Ryan.

00:17:31.829 --> 00:17:34.829
I'm here because we think he can help us.

00:17:34.829 --> 00:17:38.269
Thanks to his influence with a number of senators,

00:17:38.269 --> 00:17:42.269
your father's crucial to Congress passing anti-vigilante legislation.

00:17:42.269 --> 00:17:44.269
But right now he's in serious danger.

00:17:44.269 --> 00:17:45.269
We need to get him on.

00:17:45.269 --> 00:17:47.269
off that farm and away from Clark Kent.

00:17:47.269 --> 00:17:49.269
Clark.

00:17:49.269 --> 00:17:51.269
Kent is a vigilante.

00:17:51.269 --> 00:17:53.269
He sympathizer.

00:17:53.269 --> 00:17:56.269
Whether he knows it or not, he's helping agitators

00:17:56.269 --> 00:18:00.269
who want nothing more to stop your father from completing his current mission.

00:18:00.269 --> 00:18:07.549
It's a very serious accusation.

00:18:07.549 --> 00:18:09.549
Do you have proof?

00:18:09.549 --> 00:18:16.799
Give this to your father.

00:18:16.799 --> 00:18:19.799
Why not just deliver it to him yourself?

00:18:19.799 --> 00:18:22.799
We don't want to arouse Kent's suspicions.

00:18:22.799 --> 00:18:25.779
For your father's protection, it's best if he, not

00:18:25.799 --> 00:18:27.799
not know that you got this from me.

00:18:27.799 --> 00:18:29.799
Just tell him he found it on the farm.

00:18:29.799 --> 00:18:42.869
He'll know what to do.

00:18:42.869 --> 00:18:44.869
Could you also plant this on him?

00:18:44.869 --> 00:18:47.869
It's a homing device. It'll help us track and protect him.

00:18:47.869 --> 00:18:55.059
The U.S. Army is depending on you, Lucy.

00:18:55.059 --> 00:18:56.059
So is your father.

00:18:56.059 --> 00:19:03.819
You can count on me.

00:19:03.819 --> 00:19:05.819
Go make your father proud.

00:19:05.819 --> 00:19:22.650
I intercepted a suicide squad transmission.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:26.650
Flag's planning on killing someone, but we need to decode this before he does.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:34.509
Ah, and Chloe would have this finish like yesterday.

00:19:34.509 --> 00:19:35.509
Oliver, I'm trying to.

00:19:35.509 --> 00:19:38.509
help you, and you keep acting like I'm the enemy.

00:19:38.509 --> 00:19:39.509
Well, you know what?

00:19:39.509 --> 00:19:41.509
I'm just trying to get used to all the changes around here, okay?

00:19:41.509 --> 00:19:46.210
Look, I come here and I think of Chloe, all right.

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.210
I think of all the time that I spend here with her,

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:58.859
and I just, it's hard for me being here with someone else, okay?

00:19:58.859 --> 00:20:04.609
And I'm not trying to take her place, Oliver.

00:20:04.609 --> 00:20:09.609
But at some point, you need to start treating me like I'm on your side.

00:20:09.609 --> 00:20:30.059
General, list completed and accounted for, sir.

00:20:30.059 --> 00:20:50.240
Clark, have a seat, son.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:21:07.099
Have a seat, son. Let's get down to brass tax.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:12.220
Lois likes to date, men of action, men who make the news.

00:21:12.819 --> 00:21:16.259
Now, you, clerk, you just report the news.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.599
Why would she be possibly interested in you?

00:21:22.769 --> 00:21:23.769
Why don't you ask her, sir?

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:29.420
I asked somebody at the Pentagon instead.

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.230
Guess what he came up with.

00:21:37.609 --> 00:21:38.930
Nobody's records that clean.

